title Fold AB -- the dependent cluster, and the absentee below the fold line
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every REDS row that reads as open by a bare grep is an artifact of a closed-range fold -- %67, %69, %72, %73, %80, %83, %93, %102, %108, %109 each carry their CLOSED row in crux/archive/. The ledger stands at 110 rows, none open. No red preempts constructive work this lap.
think Council rota, lap index 590 kyri logs mod 27 -> item 23, context/specs/20260627-102012_one-clock-naming-law.md. Deep-read. Its law is why this arc can be read at all: one clock, later is larger, so thirty folds sort into the order they happened without a single renumbering. The same discipline the fold applies to code -- one text, reached from where it is needed, rather than a copy per site.
think The running thread from fold AA named the crux by measurement: run_dependent at 43 rungs by 35 lines, 1470 carried. The carry scan confirmed it on metal before anything moved.
think Hashing every run_dependent on the ladder found sixty-seven bodies at eleven distinct lengths, forty-three of them byte for byte alike. The other twenty-four are the arc's own memory of the walk growing, and none can be brought home.
think Fold Z's rule ran BEFORE scope was chosen this time -- read the reach closure first. run_dependent reaches six symbols. fixed_argv_words, inherited, and outcome_name already stood public in all forty-three. stand_taking_and_returning_reach was already a fold-L delegate needing only the word pub.
think The remaining two turned out to be real bodies standing in the very same cohort. inherited_at_first_breath hashed to one text across exactly the identical forty-three files at thirty lines apiece; slot_from_argv hashed to one text across fifty-nine. One reading bought three folds.
think The fifty-nine asked the lap's real question. Its sixteen extra rungs are cohort, cycle, confer, entrust, gap and the rest -- precisely the modules ladder_checks.rye imports. Folding them would have a rung the harness reaches for reach back through the harness. So the fold line is the widest family standing ABOVE the harness, and the sixteen stay home for a reason no earlier absentee had.
think Wrote the three bodies into caravan/ladder_checks.rye reaching everything through the rung handed in, widened three helpers across the forty-three plus reachable_between in reclaim.rye, replaced the bodies with delegates, then repinned the meter and its ceiling.
obs The arithmetic was measured rather than predicted and closed with no remainder. Out went 42x35 plus 42x30 plus 58x15 at 3,600; back came 42x3 plus 42x7 plus 42x3 plus 15x15 at 771; the fall of 2,829 is the largest this arc has taken, and the meter read 112,761 -> 109,932 exactly.
obs Carrying families held at 706 for two reasons that cancel. slot_from_argv split into delegates above the line and bodies below, gaining a family; widening reachable_between in reclaim.rye healed a two-rung private family into the forty-two-rung public one, leaving a singleton that carries nothing. Fold Z's split-by-the-word-pub recurred and closed incidentally, which is what a paid ladder looks like.
obs The scan's ceiling chain had been reciting figures four folds stale. Rather than extend a list that drifts on every fold, the chain now stops naming figures and points at the default beside the carry the scan prints -- REDS %110's lesson applied to a comment instead of a claim line.
